# Production Improvements for Arb Scanner

5 improvements to harden the arb detector for real-world usage: top-N fallback odds, rejected candidate logging, a small loop optimization, and confirming stale-odds protection.

---

## Proposed Changes

### Arb Detector

#### [MODIFY] [arb_detector.py](file:///c:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/engine/arb_detector.py)

**Improvement 1 — Top-N odds per selection (fallback candidates)**

Replace [_get_best_odds_by_selection](file:///c:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/engine/arb_detector.py#33-48) which currently keeps only 1 best price per selection. New function `_get_top_n_odds_by_selection` will keep the top 3 (configurable) odds per selection from distinct operators, sorted best-first.

```diff
-def _get_best_odds_by_selection(odds_list) -> dict[str, NormalizedOdds]:
-    # keeps single best
+def _get_top_n_odds_by_selection(odds_list, top_n=3) -> dict[str, list[NormalizedOdds]]:
+    # keeps top N from distinct operators, sorted best-first
```

Update [find_2way_arbs](file:///c:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/engine/arb_detector.py#107-180) and [find_3way_arbs](file:///c:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/engine/arb_detector.py#182-256) to use `[0]` (the best) from the returned lists. The underlying arb detection logic stays the same — we just now have fallback data available for future use (e.g., the paper trade rechecker could try fallback operators if the primary leg disappears).

**Improvement 3 — Log rejected arb candidates**

Add a summary log at the end of [find_2way_arbs](file:///c:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/engine/arb_detector.py#107-180) and [find_3way_arbs](file:///c:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/engine/arb_detector.py#182-256) counting how many candidates were rejected and why (below threshold, above threshold/palp, same operator). This gives visibility into "near miss" arbs without flooding logs.

```python
logger.info(f"2-WAY scan: {found} arbs found, {below_threshold} below min, {above_threshold} above max, {same_operator} same-operator")
```

**Improvement 4 — Move `market_key` outside loop**

In both [find_2way_arbs](file:///c:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/engine/arb_detector.py#107-180) and [find_3way_arbs](file:///c:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/engine/arb_detector.py#182-256), `market_key = odds_list[0].market_key` is already outside the pair loops (line 130), so this is actually correct. But we can extract it earlier and pass it to validation for clarity.

---

### Risk Filters

#### [MODIFY] [risk_filters.py](file:///c:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/engine/risk_filters.py)

**Improvement 5 — Confirm stale odds protection**

✅ Already implemented at lines 32-59. [filter_stale_odds](file:///c:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/engine/risk_filters.py#32-60) rejects any leg older than:
- **60 seconds** for prematch
- **10 seconds** for live markets

No code change needed here. The protection is already in `ALL_FILTERS` and runs on every arb.

**Improvement 3 (continued) — Add filter rejection summary**

Upgrade [apply_all_filters](file:///c:/Users/ahmed/OneDrive/Desktop/sportsarb/backend/engine/risk_filters.py#157-183) to accumulate rejection counts by filter name, then log a single summary line:

```python
logger.info(f"Risk filters: 5/8 passed | rejected by: stale_odds=2, suspended=1")
```

This replaces the existing `logger.debug` per-rejection with both the debug line (kept) and a summary `logger.info`.

---

### Improvement 2 — Operator Diversity (SKIPPED)

Per your note, this is optional. Skipping for now but the top-N change lays the groundwork — future code could iterate fallback operators sorted by reliability ranking.

